-10µM narrative range not a second measurement; Drug removed before recovery/readout; Drug exposure before removal: 48 h","DOI":"10.1021/mp200597r","Year":2012,"Type":"IC50"},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-052242","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"VAAP","Cell_line":"HepG2","Time(h)":48,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":0.14,"IC50_Dark_value":0.14,"Method":"MTT","Notes":"Recovery after drug removal (h): 24; Numerical source qualification: Specific line-specific ACHP13.99/10.25/5.75/10.24µM retained; approximate5-10µM narrative range not a second measurement; Drug removed before recovery/readout; Drug exposure before removal: 48 h","DOI":"10.1021/mp200597r","Year":2012,"Type":"IC50"}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"cisPt(VPA)2","value":0.25,"value_relation":"=","std":0.03,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"200 mM NaCl","temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1016/j.bcp.2015.04.003","year":2015,"record_id":"MLDB-002158","detection":"FAAS","method_description":"To determine the partition coefficient (P) the shake flask method was used. Octanol-saturated water (OSW) and water-saturated octanol (WSO) were prepared using analytical grade octanol and 0.2 M aqueous NaCl solution (to suppress hydrolysis of the chlorido complexes). Compounds were first dissolved in DMF (compounds cisPt(Ac)(VPA) and cisPt(VPA)2) or water (cisPt(Ac)2 and cisplatin). Mixing was done by vortexing for 30 min at room temperature to establish the partition equilibrium. To separate the phases, centrifugation was done at 3000 × g for 5 min. The aqueous layer was carefully separated from the octanol layer for platinum analysis. Pt was quantified from aliquots taken from the octanol-saturated aqueous samples before and after partition by FAAS. Partition coefficients of Pt complexes were calculated using the equation log P = log ([Pt]WSO/[Pt]OSW)."}]}